    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0123" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg29"/>

                <head>No. 26.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tree to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 185.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I understand that the newly-established
                    wires connecting Brussels with Paris by telephone were tried a day or two since,
                    and that the trials were perfectly successful. The line will be handed over to
                    the public use within a few days.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lambert Tree.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
